.Dd August 16, 2026
.Dt FILEES-INSTALL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm filees-install
.Nd update FileES server binaries from a signed FILEES-BIN repository
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar file
.Op Fl -check-config
.Op Fl -check Op Ar release
.Op Fl -dry-run Op Ar release
.Op Fl -apply Op Ar release
.Op Fl -adopt Op Ar release
.Op Fl -rollback
.Op Fl -revert-to Ar release
.Op Fl -purge
.Op Fl -wipe-state
.Op Fl -allow-rollback
.Op Fl -yes
.Op Fl -talkative
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
updates installed FileES server binaries from a separate binary release
repository.
It is not a package manager and does not create a local Subversion working
copy.
It fetches channel and manifest documents with
.Cm svn cat ,
verifies the OpenBSD signify signature against a public key embedded at
build time, checks SHA-256 hashes, records a durable pre-image journal,
and replaces targets atomically.
.Pp
Manifest schema v2 signs owner, group and full mode, including set-id bits.
Install and rollback restore content, UID, GID and mode.
The apply lock is exclusive; a
.Dv SIGSTOP
then
.Dv SIGKILL
chaos test on an unlocked earlier build panicked the OpenBSD kernel.
.Pp
.Fl -adopt
records an existing installation as the managed baseline.
It changes no files and accepts the host only when every managed path
matches the signed hash, owner, group and mode.
.Pp
A release older than the recorded high-water mark is refused unless
.Fl -allow-rollback
is also given.
That flag is a deliberate administrative act, never the ordinary update.
.Pp
Operator configurations are not replaced by examples. Explicit signed
configuration contracts may trigger journalled, selective migrations of
.Pa /etc/filees/server.json
and
.Pa /etc/filees/public-links.json .
Unknown fields and custom storage paths are preserved.
.Pp
The
.Ic public_downloads_dir
key in the
.Ic install
section chooses the base for migrating legacy Public Shares temporary roots.
Default:
.Pa /var/filees-downloads .
Authority staging and frontend cache remain independently configurable in
their JSON files. Apply checks capacity and prepares private directories;
check and dry-run do not provision them. Existing metadata is not silently
corrected and old caches are not deleted.
.Pp
An older running installer must first update its binary with the existing
config, then be invoked again after adding the new key. Review the migration
plan and apply the same signed release before restarting Public Shares.
The release includes examples/public-storage-migration.md with this bridge.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar file
Read
.Xr filees-install 8
configuration from
.Ar file .
The default is
.Pa /etc/filees/install.conf .
.It Fl -check-config
Print the resolved configuration and exit.
.It Fl -check
Fetch the channel and print the install plan without downloading payloads.
.It Fl -dry-run
Build the full plan, including config-contract drift, without installing.
.It Fl -apply
Download, verify, stage, journal and install the channel head or
.Ar release .
.It Fl -adopt
Verify and adopt without modification.
.It Fl -rollback
Restore the previous locally installed release from the journalled
pre-image.
.It Fl -revert-to Ar release
Install a named release such as
.Cm r543 .
.It Fl -purge
Remove files this installer manages.
Keeps
.Pa /var/filees
and
.Pa /etc/filees
unless
.Fl -wipe-state
is also given.
.It Fl -allow-rollback
Permit installing a release older than the local high-water mark.
.It Fl -yes
Answer yes to interactive prompts.
.It Fl -talkative
Print
.Sq Li [SECURITY]
unveil and pledge diagnostics.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/filees/install.conf
Updater configuration.
.It Pa /var/filees/install-state
Recorded release, high-water mark and journal.
.It Pa /var/run/filees-install.lock
Exclusive apply lock.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Adopt a host that already matches signed r543:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ doas filees-install --adopt r543
.Ed
.Pp
Plan and apply the configured channel:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ doas filees-install --dry-run
$ doas filees-install --apply
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr filees 7 ,
.Xr signify 1 ,
.Xr svn 1
